# Agent Source Awareness (Strict)

Before making any code change, always do all checks below:

1. Read `docs/senior-md/` and active rules in `.cursor/rules/`.
2. Read the target file(s) completely and inspect adjacent call sites.
3. Validate assumptions with project scripts (`type-check`, `lint`, relevant tests).
4. Keep changes surgical: no unrelated refactors, no style churn.
5. If uncertain about behavior or scope, ask instead of guessing.

## Common mistakes to avoid

- Changing APIs without updating all call sites.
- Introducing `any` in production code when concrete types are available.
- Silent behavior changes without tests or verification.
- Mixing unrelated cleanup into a feature/fix diff.
- Creating temporary docs/reports that should not persist.
